nodes.body:
@LopezCastroRoberto Thanks for the pointer! You're right that the stock column includes the as_fp32_logits upcast, so it overstates the stock path's cost once #62172 lands.

For this PR we'd like to keep decode_topk. The specialized decode row-shards the indexers, so a rank selects at most 48 rows (batch 32). In that range, decode_topk is ahead of the stock path at every shape except 65,536 columns with 1/8 valid. At 48–64 rows the faster one at most shapes is DeepSelect, not cooperative_topk. decode_topk also covers the candidate source's block selection.

The choice is made in one place in the specialized indexer (supports_decode_topk in indexer.py). So if BF16 cooperative_topk or DeepSelect turns out faster after #62172, switching is a small follow-up, and we're happy for that to be decided after this PR.

